---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import clientLogos from '../assets/about/logos.png';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About · James Samuel-Camps" 
  description="Lead Product Designer with over 15 years experience building complex B2B/B2C fintech infrastructure, design systems, and UI architecture."
>
  <div class="container-prose">
    <header class="about-header">
      <span class="badge-role">Lead Product Designer</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">About James Samuel-Camps</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose about-content">
      <h2>Personal Profile</h2>
      <p>
        I’m a Lead Product Designer with over 15 years of experience building complex B2B/B2C fintech infrastructure, design systems, and scalable UI architecture. Currently based in the UK, open to new opportunities, and building <strong><a href="https://github.com/jamessamuelcamps/tilia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tilia</a></strong>, a free UX research platform for solo practitioners, small product teams, and founders.
      </p>

      <h2>Background & Mindset</h2>
      <p>
        My path into product design wasn’t standard. I studied magazine journalism, spending my early career in trend forecasting and editorial design. That background taught me two critical skills that define my approach today: <strong>separating long-term human behaviour from short-term fads</strong>, and <strong>mastering strict information hierarchy</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In fintech, where software is often weighed down by legacy code and heavy regulatory constraints, I use those skills to abstract messy logic into simple, intuitive user mental models.
      </p>

      <h2>Approach to Leadership</h2>
      <p>
        I’m passionate about mentoring and supporting my team, with a strong belief in trust-based management. I avoid micromanagement, both giving and receiving; it stifles growth and never leads to the results you’re looking for.
      </p>
      <p>
        While I see myself as accountable for my team’s development, I encourage them to take charge of their own paths, with me providing guidance as needed. My feedback style is adaptable, with a preference for real-time calls for in-depth discussions.
      </p>

      <h2>How I Operate</h2>
      
      <h3>Logic over Theatre</h3>
      <p>
        I value outcomes over performative design rituals. I prefer fast, informed assumptions, quick prototypes, and immediate testing over endless “design by committee.” Process should serve product velocity, not slow it down.
      </p>

      <h3>Systems Architecture</h3>
      <p>
        I am drawn to the structural layer of product design. I turn back-end technical complexity into clear, maintainable design systems and self-service component libraries. Solid documentation and UI systems are business assets that save hundreds of engineering hours.
      </p>

      <h3>Autonomy, Trust & Momentum</h3>
      <p>
        I believe in tight, cross-functional alignment early on; aligning with product, risk, and engineering on what needs to be solved. Once aligned, I execute with high autonomy and protect the team’s maker-time so we can focus on shipping high-quality software quickly.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <div class="clients-section">
        <p class="clients-title">I’ve previously worked with</p>
        <figure class="clients-logos">
          <Image
            src={clientLogos}
            alt="Clients including Tide, Moneybox, YouLend, and more"
            class="logos-img"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="contact-box">
        <h3>Get in Touch</h3>
        <p>
          Currently open to new opportunities and design consulting.
        </p>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="mailto:hello@james-sc.co.uk" class="btn btn-primary">Email Me</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamessc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/jamessamuelcamps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .badge-role {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .clients-section {
    margin: var(--space-10) 0;
  }

  .clients-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .clients-logos {
    padding: var(--space-6) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .logos-img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    filter: grayscale(100%);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .contact-box {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>

